WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.280
The first season of HBO's Watchmen has proven
to be complex, riveting, and sometimes, a

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:06.780
little bit confusing.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.020
It's impossible for a story like this to not
end with some unanswered questions, so here

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.940
are the biggest ones we came away with.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:19.340
Warning: Like having a conversation with Dr.
Manhattan, you will be spoiled.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:25.520
Adrian Veidt spends almost a decade essentially
imprisoned on Europa We see his time there

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.480
throughout the season, interspersed with events
in Tulsa.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.660
By the season finale, it's clear what's going
on in Oklahoma is not happening at the same

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.620
time as Veidt's adventures on Jupiter's most
lively moon.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:42.640
The proof is the golden "statue" of Veidt
that Angela Abar and Laurie Blake notice when

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.180
they interview Lady Trieu.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:50.260
Laurie comments on how old he looks in the
recreation, and it's because it's not a statue.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.380
When Trieu sends a ship to rescue Veidt from
Europa, he's preserved for the trip by being

00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:00.940
encased in a golden shell, and the instructions
he's given insist he put his hands on his

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.520
hips before the procedure.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:08.039
Trieu clearly keeps him on display for a while
before reviving him just in time to show him

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.680
her master plan in action.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.300
Just how long is not entirely clear.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.340
When Doctor Manhattan teleports Adrian Veidt,
Laurie Blake, and Looking Glass to Veidt's

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.840
base in Antarctica, it doesn't take much for
Veidt to convince the others that Lady Trieu's

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:26.130
plan to become the next Doctor Manhattan needs
to be stopped.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.240
Veidt says his daughter won't actually save
the world, as she claims, because:

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:36.639
"She is clearly a raging narcissist whose
ambition knows no limits.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:37.920
It's hubris.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.440
Literal hubris."

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.500
Trieu definitely does seem to fit that bill.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:47.079
She doesn't hesitate to kill the leaders of
the Kavalry and doesn't seem the least bit

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:47.580
shaken.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:50.940
She's dishonest, manipulative and ruthless.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:56.040
Yet all those things could be said about Veidt,
who does genuinely hope to save humanity with

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.400
his act of genocide at the end of the original
comic book series.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:02.440
"Takes one to know one."

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:11.300
It could be that if Trieu's plan had worked,
she could have become some awful dictator.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:16.420
It's also possible that Trieu would have done
exactly what she said and used her new powers

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:17.660
to make the world a better place.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.200
It's kinda what her dad did, right?

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.740
In episode 4, Angela, in her Sister Night
guise, chases down a costumed figure who douses

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.700
himself in oil, drops to the pavement and
slides away into a storm drain.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.690
The audience's reaction seemed to be pretty
similar to Angela's:

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:35.420
"What the f---?"

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:41.480
Viewers had to be expecting to get some sort
of explanation or at least a clue as to who

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:46.379
this mysterious "Lube Man" was in the finale,
but he wasn't even mentioned.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.680
The show's creators did offer some clue as
to his identity, though.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:55.500
HBO has been publishing supplemental materials
on its website under the title "Peteypedia,"

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.720
written in the world of the show by FBI agent
Dale Petey.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.540
The last entry isn't credited to Petey, however.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:06.620
It's credited to an FBI deputy director, who
explains that Petey is no longer employed

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:12.020
by the FBI because of his obsession with masked
vigilantes and his meandering reports.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.500
Among the possessions removed from his office?

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.700
"[...] a jug of what appears to be some kind
of canola oil."

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:24.700
When we first meet Will Reeves, he's over
100 years old, retired from his secret life

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:29.080
as Hooded Justice, but spurred back to action
after meeting Doctor Manhattan.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.640
For someone who's lived for over a century,
he's in miraculously good health.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:37.860
Even though he claims to be wheelchair-bound
at first, we eventually learn he's perfectly

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.900
capable of walking all on his own.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:44.980
The most obvious answer to how Reeves is in
such good health is Lady Trieu.

00:03:45.409 --> 00:03:50.560
She's a scientific genius who has no compunctions
about using unconventional methods to achieve

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:51.060
her goals.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.800
Someone like Trieu seems more than capable
of keeping a man alive and healthy longer

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:56.300
than most.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.720
Or maybe Hooded Justice is just made of stronger
stuff than the rest of us.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:06.180
At first, the message from Doctor Manhattan
that Will relays to Angela in the movie theater

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.500
seems like nonsense.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.180
"You can't make an omelet without breaking
a couple eggs."

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.200
"What the hell's that supposed to mean?"

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:21.039
But when Angela goes to clean up the egg carton
she slammed on the kitchen floor during her

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.680
argument with Jon, she remembers Jon telling
her "Watch the eggs."

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:29.360
Lo and behold, one egg remains unbroken.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:34.840
During Angela's first meeting with Jon, he
explained he could transfer his power into

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.340
an egg that would grant someone else who ate
it his abilities.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:45.080
"I suppose I could transfer my atomic components
into some sort of organic material."

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.560
Angela takes the egg to her backyard and downs
it.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:53.960
She slowly reaches out to the water of her
pool to see if she'll be able to walk on water

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:54.760
like Jon.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.040
Then the screen goes black.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.760
Will Angela be the new Doctor Manhattan?

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.620
We're intentionally left in the dark on that
question.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:08.480
Upon his return to Earth, Adrian Veidt isn't
met with the praise and forgiveness he expects.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:14.000
"May I ask you what everybody thinks happened
to him?"

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:15.580
"Aw, nobody cares."

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:21.520
Armed with the recordings Veidt made for President
Robert Redford, Laurie Blake and Looking Glass

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.960
insist on arresting Veidt for his crimes.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.920
Veidt laughs at the idea, but Looking Glass
knocks him out cold.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:32.880
Assuming they return to the U.S. with Veidt
and the proof of his crimes, the whole world

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:38.050
will presumably learn the peace forged after
what was thought to be an assault by extra-dimensional

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:43.100
aliens was a lie, and that the U.S. president
was secretly handpicked from the shadows.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.320
Will the Cold War reignite?

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:50.780
Or, alternatively, will Veidt's recordings
prove no more effective than Rorschach's journal?

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:56.039
Will most people find the revelations too
fantastic to be true and ignore them as crazy

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.040
conspiracy theories?

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:02.039
Many of these questions could be answered
in a second season of Watchmen, but show creator

00:06:02.039 --> 00:06:07.370
Damon Lindelof has said repeatedly he wanted
the first season to tell one self-contained

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.900
story, just as the original comic series did.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:15.430
He hasn't completely ruled out future seasons,
though he seems adamant he won't be a part

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:19.480
of it unless there's another story he eventually
wants to tell in the world of Watchmen.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:24.699
He also says he's open to the idea of stepping
back and letting someone else tackle another

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:25.200
season.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.460
So will there be a season two of Watchmen?

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:37.640
"You avoided answering by saying, 'Nothing
ever ends.'"

